  "README.md": "# my-app

Stack: SvelteKit, Svelte 5, Sass, Tailwind CSS, Svelte runes store, Axios, Vitest, ESLint, Prettier, Husky, lint-staged, SEO, llms.txt.

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
npm install
npm run dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`npm run build\`
- \`npm run preview\`
- \`npm run prepare\`
- \`npm run test\`
- \`npm run lint\`
- \`npm run format\`
- \`npm run format:check\`

## API client

Copy \`.env.example\` to \`.env\` and set \`VITE_API_URL\`. Import the client from \`src/api/client\`.

## Git hooks

The pre-commit hook runs lint-staged on staged files (lint-staged needs Node.js 22.22.1 or newer). Hooks are installed by \`prepare\` during install, which needs a git repository: after \`git init\`, run the install once more.

## SEO

Set \`SITE_URL\` to your public origin (defaults to \`https://example.com\`). It is used for canonical URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt and llms.txt.

## Push to GitHub

Create an empty repository on GitHub, then:

\`\`\`bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/my-app.git
git push -u origin main
\`\`\`
