  "README.md": "# my-app

Stack: Vue 3, Vite, Sass, Tailwind CSS, Pinia, Vue Router, Axios, Vitest, Testing Library, ESLint, Prettier, Husky, lint-staged, SEO, llms.txt.

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
npm install
npm run dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`npm run build\`
- \`npm run preview\`
- \`npm run test\`
- \`npm run lint\`
- \`npm run format\`
- \`npm run format:check\`
- \`npm run prepare\`

## API client

Copy \`.env.example\` to \`.env\` and set \`VITE_API_URL\`. Import the client from \`src/api/client\`.

## Git hooks

The pre-commit hook runs lint-staged on staged files (lint-staged needs Node.js 22.22.1 or newer). Hooks are installed by \`prepare\` during install, which needs a git repository: after \`git init\`, run the install once more.

## SEO

Replace \`https://example.com\` in \`index.html\` and \`public/\` with your domain. This is a client-rendered app: crawlers that do not run JavaScript (social previews, most AI crawlers) only see the static tags in \`index.html\`. For per-page SEO use a meta-framework (Next.js, Nuxt, SvelteKit, Astro).

## Push to GitHub

Create an empty repository on GitHub, then:

\`\`\`bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/my-app.git
git push -u origin main
\`\`\`
